A||||13||Howard_Sacks||Is my fiero totaled?||||5||
Z||000000||Howard_Sacks||04-03-2001||03:55 PM||||While driving to my first autocross this past sunday I was hit on i95 by a van.  I don't remember much about the accident because it happened so fast but for those who are curious:<P>I was in the left middle lane, the van was in the passing lane<P>I was doing about 60-65, the van was doing less, when I was about to pass the van he cut sharply and immediately into my lane without using a signal or giving me enough time to react. <P>I cut harshly into the right center lane and got loose. While trying to settle my fiero, I was hit again by the van and then lost complete control.<P>I have posted a movie of my car after the accident at <A HREF="http://www.saturnet.net/fiero.mov" TARGET=_blank>www.saturnet.net/fiero.mov</A>   (you need quicktime to view it)  You only need to view half of it, because when I originally shot and encoded the video, I thought I was going to try to sell it.  So the 2nd half is of my engine's new manifold lines and the new cross-drilled and vented rotors.  But now I think I'm going to keep it temporarily.<P>My question for the group is, is the car salvageable or should I just swap the engine and new breaks into a donor?<P><BR>Thank you,<P>Howard Sacks<BR>87GT Auto Hurt Bad<BR>86GT 4-spd Dead Engine (was going to be a club racer)||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||04-03-2001||04:09 PM||||well.. uum welcome to the forum sorry it had to start out like this!<P>uum yeah.. your insurance company will probly total your ride. the b-pillar looks pushed in and the floor board looks bent.. since these are structural assemblies.. your probly toast. well looks like a good time for the swap you mentioned...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||04-03-2001||04:22 PM||||Yeah I didnt think it was that bad till the screen panned up over the drivers side fender to the door (1/4 way through) Looks like its totaled, sorry.<P>Just make sure you get enough to buy another GT!<P><p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000003||c m west||04-03-2001||04:40 PM||||think of it as your parts telling you to put them into a different car - donor time, if you need any help let us know.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Howard_Sacks||04-03-2001||04:44 PM||||&gt;uum yeah.. your insurance company will probly total your ride. the b-pillar looks pushed in and the floor board looks bent..<P>I don't have collision on my car, just liability, and the police officer was giving me a hard time at the scene of the accident.  I'm not sure why, maybe kid in a sports car. I'm hoping for the best, but bracing for the worst. I'm getting the report tommorow so I'll see who they determine to be at fault. I'm actually lucky it wasn't in NJ since we have "no fault" and they determine everything to be both driver's fault.  I wasn't able to talk to the driver of the van becuase paramedics showed up before I could get out of the car so I hope he has insurance.<P>&gt; since these are<BR>&gt;structural assemblies.. your probly toast. well looks like a good time for the swap you mentioned... <P>I was hoping to be able to drive this back to NJ(I'm at college in providence RI).  It drove straight from the scene of the accident back to the parking lot I use.  Should I have the car towed?<P><BR>Thanks for the help<p>[This message has been edited by Howard_Sacks (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||04-03-2001||04:56 PM||||Kid in a sports car, you might as well forget it.  When I had an accident in my first formula, it was so obviously not my fault, but they immediately said that I was speeding and it was a "no fault" accident.  The cop was a major prick.  He even cited skid marks when the pavement was wet!<P>I talked to a lawyer and he told me that they probably won't even believe me over this sweet poor innocent 90 year old lady.  Sorry it doesn't look good for you, I would get it towed also.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||04-03-2001||05:01 PM||||YOU DROVE IT!! you must ahve been really fortunate.. the coolant tubes under the car didn't split... well if the coolant tubes aren't split.. the frame may not be as thrashedas the pics make it look... ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Howard_Sacks||04-03-2001||05:27 PM||||Black 88GT:  My father is talking with friends of his in the area to see if they know any good attorneys up here.  The first person on the scene was a "correction officer" who wanted to play cop.  He wouldn't tell me if he was a police officer (At the time I didn't know what a correction officer was I just knew his uniform didn't say police) yelled at me when I didn't then give him my license and registration since he refused to answer if he was a police officer.  Then he threatened to put me in "cuffs" and send me to jail if I continued to look at my car and didn't stand next to the median.  The state police trooper started to go threw my luggage when I opened my trunk to find out why I lost juice. (my battery was jarred loose)<P>1fst2m6: the frame is thrashed, the driver's seat is now tilted, the e break doesn't come up properly now due to the door being bent in.  I was hoping someone was going to post I could bring this to a "frame shop" and just replace the door.  I don't care about cosmetics at this point, but I don't want a car that isn't safe.  <P>I probably should get it towed since the oil pressure is now pinned and the temp gauge does not work.  What's the most cost effective way to do this?<P>I don't know if this is against forum etiquette but 1fst2m6, do you still sell the aluminum cradle bushings?  No offense meant Eric, but I'm a poor college student :-(  If I do the swap I'll order the transmission mounts from you guys.<P><BR>Thank you again for the advice||||reg||1
Z||000008||stsmithgt||04-03-2001||07:03 PM||||I feel your PAIN about the cops giving you a hard time.  I'm not a kid, but I still got the sharp end of the stick with some threats of being hauled off to jail.  The punk in the Caddy got a lot more respect and it wasn't even his car or even his rental.  He was just someones gopher taking back to the airport. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> That search the troop did doesn't sound legal either though it might be in an accident, but I doubt it. NOT that there was something to HIDE. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
