Z||000010||Mach10||04-04-2001||02:19 AM||||OUCH! Liability only?!?<BR>I feel your pain. My suggestion to you would be to point out the type of damage, and state that you had signalled intention to pass, and was PASSING. If he hits you again AFTER the initial hit, state that it was due to the first impact and that the car was thrown out of your control. In our area, if some ass-clown tries that even WITH turn signals, our insurance company will find him 75% at fault. If he didn't signal, then its a full 100%. I almost got nailed when I totalled my car when I hit a REFRIDGERATOR DOOR that some as$C|oWn left in the highway, just over the crest of a bridge. Spud out, slammed into a concrete barrier, at about 60mph. Managed to flag down a snow-plow and get him to take a statement. As it was, Autopac nailed me 100%, which I fought like a bastard. I got 'em down to No Fault, with only the $200 deductible. I was lucky. Your best bet would be a witness, if you can find one. <BR>Sorry!<BR>That REALLY sucks.||216.81.4.225||reg||11
Z||000011||tgowens||04-04-2001||04:01 AM||||Howard,<P>I would take that to a body shop and let them take a look at that side damage........it is possible that the frame is not that significantly damaged however, you will need a new door (as well as a few other parts).................removing the front fascia will tell you if the front end has been pushed back any but from the picture it doesn't look like it recieved any damage.....<P>Like I said, I would let a body/frame shop take a look........||||reg||1
Z||000012||Howard_Sacks||04-04-2001||10:58 PM||||Alright guys,  thanks a lot for the help.  If it's nice out tomorrow I'm going to try to get it back to jersey from providence.  If it's raining or looks like it's going to rain, I'm going to have to wait since I'm missing the window.  <P>1fst2m4: I had to drive it or else it would have got impounded.  I would have got out and pushed it if I had to. I got under the car today.  None of the pipes running under are damaged.  Is the cooling tube the pipe that has the jackpoint on it?<P>stsmithgt: There was nothing to hide but I don't like illegal searches.  Although now that I think about it, my passenger was a musician so you never know.<P>mach10:  I had a passenger who witnessed the 2nd hit, but I don't think the cop believed us.  State police still didn't have the report finished today so I don't know who they're faulting.  I was told to call back tomorrow.  I'm kicking myself in the but for not taking down the name of someone who saw the accident and stopped to ask us if we were all right.<P>tgowens:  unfortunately I don't know any reputable body shops in providence.  I do know some in jersey.  Does anyone know of any in providence before I take the drive?<P><BR>If I get this thing down, I'm going to put the engine into my other GT, and most likely I'm going to be parting it out. If anyone has requests for parts email me and I'll put you first on the list.  I don't think there's one good panel on the drivers side but other than that the car's pretty good.  GT wheels or a spoiler anyone?<P><BR>Thank you,<P><BR>Howard<BR>87GT Auto -One last trip<BR>86GT 4spd -Hopefully getting an engine||||reg||1
